{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3365","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3365","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3365\",\"parent_revision\":\"0cbb3e82291fa9d8938f25c51ef10d5c487568e22499a5ced6957c88b10bdf13\",\"root_revision\":\"0cbb3e82291fa9d8938f25c51ef10d5c487568e22499a5ced6957c88b10bdf13\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-01\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\noperations.add_item's integer-ID backend path (GitHub/SQLite/Memory) calls _try_create_github_issue, which calls try_get_github(repo). SQLiteBackend.try_get_github and InMemoryBackend.try_get_github are both hardcoded to return None (\\\"has no GitHub connection\\\"), so on SQLite/Memory this call always returns None regardless of backend capability, and add_item always falls back to the local-only path: the item is stored only via backend.put_work_item() (the opaque-reference native work-item store) and never inserted into SQLite's items table or Memory's _issues dict via backend.create_issue_for_item().\\n\\nThis means a normally-created SQLite or Memory backlog item never gets a real integer issue_number in that backend's native store, so any backend-native operation keyed on issue_number (milestone assignment, labels, comments, status transitions read through _fetch_issues_graphql, etc.) can never find it. AGENTS.md's \\\"State Management\\\" section (lines 82-84) states the configured backend is \\\"the sole storage boundary for work items\\\" -- this contradicts that for SQLite/Memory on the normal add_item path.\\n\\nVerified by reading operations.py:_try_create_github_issue (calls try_get_github, returns None => \\\"GitHub unavailable -- creating local-only item\\\" warning) and both backends' try_get_github implementations directly. This predates PR #3364 (add_item/_try_create_github_issue/try_get_github are untouched by that PR) and is out of scope for a \\\"make milestones backend-agnostic\\\" slice -- the fix requires redesigning add_item's dispatch for local backends (a real local-creation path bypassing the GitHub-shaped try_get_github gate), not a milestone-specific change.\\n\\nNot a duplicate of #2287 (the parent milestone-backend-agnostic item) or the other suggested matches (#1722 token budget, #2438 artifact MCP str/int coercion, #473 MCP prompts, #3361 ty unreachable branches) -- none of those touch add_item's local-backend dispatch.\\n\\nUser-provided context: found via Codex automated review, comment at https://github.com/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/pull/3364#discussion_r3900655581 (references AGENTS.md:L82-L84).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Codex review on PR #3364 (backlog #2287 slice C, milestone backend-agnostic work)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4d0330a7ca7ef695c4aa02c793e3ffc64de30c184283cf1fce9446673a7130bd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABR0jPjw\"}"}